From c991108481fbddded6a813503aa7ca7d87c622c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: warelik <warelik@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 16:05:02 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] Add tab width bounds and tab chip settings

tabs.min_width and tabs.max_width clamp the tab width; editor and
terminal titles truncate in the middle when a maximum is set.
tab_bar.pinned_tab_chips and tab_bar.unpinned_tab_chips render the
tabs of the pinned or unpinned row as compact borderless chips.
tab_bar.max_tab_rows (default 1, 0 behaves as 1) wraps overflowing
unpinned tabs onto up to N rows when both width bounds are set; tabs
shrink within a row down to min_width, only the last allowed row
scrolls, and tabs can be dropped into a row's empty space.

The tab width regression renders an actual tab before asserting.

